<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baiju</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 1260</span> · Also known as Baiju Noyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baiju was a Mongol general who succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chormaqan">Chormaqan</a> as commander of the Mongol forces in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> about 1242. In 1243 he defeated the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykhusraw-ii">Kaykhusraw II</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kose-dag">Battle of Köse Dağ</a>, making the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> a Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. He continued to lead Mongol armies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and took part in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a>'s campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1258.</p></div>
